<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34057" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pastĭnātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the act of preparing the soil of a vineyard</i>, <i>by digging and trenching it.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pastinationem suscipere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					3, 12, 6</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">3, 13,
			4</span></i>.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>ground so
			prepared</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pastinatio vitibus conserenda est,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					11, 2, 17</span></i>
			; so <i><span class="en">id. 3, 15, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">3, 3, 15</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
